list.item:
Check the expiration dates (YYYY/MM) on the HEPCLUDEX Vial (see 
                                       Figure A
                                    ) and on the supplies for mixing and injecting HEPCLUDEX.

Wash your hands well with soap and water (see 
                                       Figure B
                                    ).

Check the powder or cake in the HEPCLUDEX Vial. The powder or cake should be a white to off-white color (see 
                                       Figure C
                                    ).

Remove the cap from the HEPCLUDEX Vial (see 
                                       Figure D
                                    ).

Remove the cap from the Sterile Water for Injection Vial (see 
                                       Figure E
                                    ).

Clean the rubber stopper of the HEPCLUDEX Vial with an alcohol swab (see 
                                       Figure F
                                    ).

With a different alcohol swab, clean the rubber stopper of the Sterile Water for Injection Vial (see 
                                       Figure G
                                    ).

Turn the Transfer Needle to the right (clockwise) onto the Syringe until it is fully connected (see 
                                       Figure H
                                    ).

Remove the needle cap from the Transfer Needle by pulling it straight off (see 
                                       Figure I
                                    ). Keep the needle cap for later use.

Insert the Transfer Needle all the way into the Sterile Water for Injection Vial by pushing it straight through the center of the rubber stopper (see 
                                       Figure J
                                    ).

With the other hand, carefully pull the plunger down until the top rim of the plunger lines up with the 1 mL marking on the Syringe (see 
                                       Figure K
                                    ).

Remove the water-filled Syringe with the Transfer Needle attached from the Sterile Water for Injection Vial by holding the Syringe body and pulling it straight up (see 
                                       Figure L
                                    ).

Pull the plunger all the way down to the 2 mL marking of the Syringe to add air to the Syringe (see 
                                       Figure M
                                    ).

Insert the Transfer Needle all the way into the HEPCLUDEX Vial by pushing it straight through the center of the rubber stopper (see 
                                       Figure N
                                    ).

Slowly push the plunger all the way up until the Syringe is empty (see 
   Figure O
).

Remove the empty Syringe with the Transfer Needle attached from the HEPCLUDEX Vial by pulling it straight up (see 
                                       Figure P
                                    ).

Using one hand, slide the Transfer Needle into its cap and scoop upwards to cover the needle (see 
                                       Figure Q
                                    ).

Slowly swirl the HEPCLUDEX Vial for a few seconds to mix the powder with the Sterile Water for Injection (see 
                                       Figure R
                                    ).

Wait for the powder to fully dissolve (see 
                                       Figure S
                                    ). This may take up to 3 minutes.

Check that the powder is fully dissolved. The medicine should look clear without any clumps or particles (see 
                                       Figure T
                                    ).

Hold the Syringe firmly (see 
                                       Figure U
                                    ).

Turn the Transfer Needle to the right (clockwise) onto the Syringe until it is fully connected (see 
                                       Figure V
                                    ).

Remove the needle cap from the Transfer Needle by pulling it straight off (see 
                                       Figure W
                                    ). Keep the needle cap for later use.

Insert the Transfer Needle all the way into the HEPCLUDEX Vial by pushing it straight through the center of the rubber stopper (see 
                                       Figure X
                                    ).

Check the plunger is pushed all the way down. If the plunger has risen, push the plunger all the way down (see 
                                       Figure Y
                                    ). All air should be pushed out of the Syringe.

While pushing down on the plunger, turn the HEPCLUDEX Vial and Syringe so that the vial is pointing upwards (see 
                                       Figure Z
                                    ).

Pull the Transfer Needle down until the needle tip is near the bottom of the rubber stopper in the vial. Check the position through the gap in the rubber stopper (see 
                                       Figure AA
                                    ).

Keep the Transfer Needle tip in place inside the HEPCLUDEX Vial (see 
                                       Figure BB
                                    ).

Carefully pull the plunger until all the medicine is removed from the HEPCLUDEX Vial (see 
                                       Figure BB
                                    ).

Before continuing, check that all the liquid medicine is removed from the HEPCLUDEX Vial (see 
                                       Figure CC
                                    ).

While holding the Syringe body and plunger in place, remove the Syringe with the Transfer Needle attached from the HEPCLUDEX Vial (see 
                                       Figure DD
                                    ).

Using one hand, slide the Transfer Needle into its cap and scoop upwards to cover the needle (see 
                                       Figure EE
                                    ).

Hold the Syringe firmly (see 
                                       Figure FF
                                    ).

Hold the Syringe firmly (see 
                                       Figure GG
                                    ).

Turn the Injection Needle to the right (clockwise) onto the Syringe until it is fully connected (see 
                                       Figure GG
                                    ).

Place the Syringe with the Injection Needle attached on a flat surface (see 
                                       Figure HH
                                    ).

To inject yourself, choose a site on your lower abdomen (stomach) or upper thighs (see 
                                       Figure II
                                    ).

If someone else is injecting the medicine for you, they can also choose the back of the upper arms (see 
                                       Figure JJ
                                    ).

Clean the injection site with a new alcohol swab (see 
                                        Figure KK
                                    ).

Gently pull back the Injection Needle safety shield (see 
                                       Figure LL
                                    ).

Carefully pull off the Injection Needle cap (see 
                                       Figure MM
                                    ) and throw it away into the household trash.

If there is a large air gap, carefully push the plunger up to remove most of the air gap at the top (see 
                                       Figure NN
                                    ).

Pinch the cleaned injection site (see 
                                       Figure OO
                                    ).

Right after the injection, place the Injection Needle safety shield on the work surface (see 
                                       Figure QQ
                                    ).

Press the needle toward the needle safety shield to cover the needle and lock the safety shield (see 
                                       Figure RR
                                    ).

If there is bleeding at the injection site, gently press a cotton ball or gauze over the injection site for several seconds (see 
                                       Figure TT
                                    ).

If you do not have an FDA-cleared sharps disposal container, you may use a household container that is:


made of heavy-duty plastic;

able to be closed with a tight-fitting, puncture-resistant lid, without sharps being able to come out;

upright and stable during use;

leak-resistant; and

properly labeled to warn of hazardous waste inside the container.
